(pygame, numpy, matplotlib, pandas, pytest), `README.md` skeleton, `pytest.ini`.
**Done when:** `pytest` runs (even with zero tests) and imports work.

## v1 — Board and rules (`game/board.py`)

Implement the full Board interface from ARCHITECTURE.md (except `hash`).

- `winner()` checks only the 4 directions through the last placed disc (fast), but
  `winning_cells()` must return the exact four cells.
- Reject illegal moves with `ValueError`.
  **Tests (`tests/test_board.py`):** horizontal, vertical, both diagonals (each for both
  players); a full board with no winner is a draw; dropping into a full column raises;
  `undo` restores the exact previous state; `from_string`/`to_string` round-trip;
  `current_player` alternates correctly; random playouts (seeded, 1000 games) never
  produce an invalid state and `winner()` agrees with a slow brute-force full-board check.
